+A 19-language override layer for DSH i18n (ja/ko/fr/...). A selected third
+language wins over DSH's native zh/en while DSH's active locale stays on
+`en`; a custom switcher row in the settings General section drives the
+selection, and the choice persists in localStorage
+(`dsh-plugin-better-locale:active`). The same languages and dictionaries are
+also registered through DSH's native language-pack API
+(`locale.addLanguage` + `locale.register(ns, locale, dict)`), so they appear
+in DSH's own Settings → General Language row as well and resolve through the
+native per-key fallback chain to `en`. Client-only plugin — the host half is
+a no-op stub. Targets dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
 
-Release procedure (internal):
+## Entry points
+
+| Entry point | Where |
+|---|---|
+| Pre-chain override seat: `ctx.locale.intercept` where the host carries it, else the rebased LocaleRuntime `lookup` patch (probe → inert no-op when neither exists) | client.js `installOverrideSeat` |
+| Custom switcher row in Settings → General (`settings.general.item`, id `better-locale`, order 10, after the locale package's own row) | client.js step 7 |
+| Override selection persisted in localStorage (`dsh-plugin-better-locale:active`, best-effort) | client.js `loadActiveFromStorage` / `setActive` |
+| `ctx.betterLocale` service so third-party plugins register their own languages and dictionaries (`inject = ['betterLocale']`) | client.js step 4 |
+| Own copy namespace `dsh-plugin-better-locale` (zh/en switcher copy) | client.js step 1 |
+| Store → locale revision refresh bridge (outlets re-derive `t` after a selection change) | client.js step 6 |
+| Native language-pack registration (belt and braces; also feeds DSH's own Language row) | client.js `registerNativeLanguages` |
+| Bundle patch (`cordis.patch.yml`, `dsh.bundle.patch`) inserting the plugin row | cordis.patch.yml |
+
+## Upstream seat request
+
+The override layer needs a public pre-chain seat and a public revision-refresh
+entry; both are private runtime internals at alpha.2 (`lookup`, `publish`).
+`patches/locale-translation-override-seat.patch` proposes the harness change
+(`ctx.locale.intercept` + `ctx.locale.refresh`) and is ready to file upstream.
+Until the seat lands, the plugin uses the rebased `lookup` patch and the
+private `publish` bump, re-probed on every mount.
+
+## Moved onto official extension points
+
+- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` is gone from `dsh.client.inject` and the
+  peer block (removed in alpha.1, DSH-0.1.2-A1-25); the client context is
+  cordis `Context` plus the owning packages' type merges.
+- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy` and `schemastery` are gone (the apiproxy
+  package was deleted at alpha.1, DSH-0.1.2-A1-01; schemastery was unused).
+- The stale `dsh-client-connection`, `dsh-client-ui-settings`,
+  `dsh-client-ui-slots` and `dsh-client-ui-primitives` peer rows are gone.
+  `dsh.client.inject` keeps the one package edge the client half depends on
+  (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-locale`, the service owner); the `slots` service
+  is sequenced by the Cordis `inject` list, and `react` / `ui-slots` /
+  `ui-primitives` / `client-store` ride the browser module baseline without
+  manifest rows.
+- Language and dictionary registration also ride the native language-pack API
+  `locale.addLanguage` / `locale.register(ns, locale, dict)`
+  (DSH-0.1.2-A1-10).
+- The package name is `@bench/dsh-bench-locale-pack`, equal to the bundle
+  row's `name` (DSH-0.1.2-A1-26).
+
+## Release procedure (internal)
 
 1. Apply the migration changes.
-2. Bump the version in package.json.
-3. Publish: `pnpm publish --force` — the registry checks are just warnings, so
